WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:03.359
Euclid's Elements, Book One, Proposition Eleven.

2
00:00:03.359 --> 00:00:08.073
Construct a segment at right angles to a given line from a given point on it.

3
00:00:08.073 --> 00:00:13.890
Given segment A B and point C on it, we are to construct from C a segment perpendicular to A B.

4
00:00:14.310 --> 00:00:17.695
Take a point D at random on segment A C.

5
00:00:17.695 --> 00:00:23.280
By Proposition Three, cut off from C B a segment C E equal to C D.

6
00:00:23.430 --> 00:00:29.620
Next, by Proposition One, on segment D E construct the equilateral triangle F D E.

7
00:00:29.770 --> 00:00:35.200
Then, by Postulate One, construct the segment F C joining vertex F to point C.

8
00:00:35.620 --> 00:00:44.178
Now compare triangles D C F and E C F: side D C equals E C, side C F is common, and base D F equals base F E.

9
00:00:44.178 --> 00:00:52.500
Therefore, by Proposition Eight, side-side-side congruence, the adjacent angles D C F and E C F are equal.

10
00:00:52.650 --> 00:01:01.140
By Definition Ten, when a segment standing on a line makes the adjacent angles equal, each angle is a right angle and the segment is perpendicular.

11
00:01:01.140 --> 00:01:07.840
Therefore segment C F has been constructed at right angles to segment A B from point C on it, as was required to do.
